---
# Every actor acts at most once, so every behaviour ends at rest with
# nothing left to do: that is the bound, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---
# Deleting a project while something else is still using it: the first
# message minting and booting the project's main thread, a save of an
# orb file from the project page, and an agent writing into the
# project's directory with the file tools. project_lifecycle treats
# Delete as one atomic step and project_main_threads never deletes; this
# flow is the interleavings between them.
#
# Checked against internal/serve supervisor.go DeleteProject, EndProject,
# Main, MainID, createWithID and claim; projects.go messageProject;
# orbs.go putOrbFile; projectdef.go ListAll, CreateEmpty, WriteFile and
# atomicWrite; cmd/bough/mode.go (a project child loads project.yml
# before it writes history, and exits when it cannot); orb/image.go
# EnsureImage (MkdirAll of the image dir, no check that the project
# still exists).
#
# This spec models the product AS IT IS, races included, so the MBT and
# browser layers can hold it to what it does. What it SHOULD do is
# listed at the bottom as the assertions the product fails today; each
# was model-checked against this spec (appended as an assertion) and
# its counterexample is in the commit that added the flow.
#
# One project "alpha", listed (GET /api/projects is ListAll on
# every call, so "listed" is yml here; the page's poll lag is
# project_lifecycle's ListCatchesUp), with a built image (cache), no MEMORY.md,
# and no main thread yet. Every other actor acts at most once, so the
# graph stays finite and small:
#
#   yml, dir  project.yml and the directory. The list (ListAll) and
#             Project() see a project only when project.yml reads; Create
#             (os.Mkdir) is refused by the directory alone.
#   stray     a file in the directory other than project.yml (MEMORY.md
#             from the save or from the agent).
#   tmp       atomicWrite's temp file (.MEMORY.md.tmp-*) sitting in the
#             directory between CreateTemp and the rename.
#   cache     ~/.bough/orbs/images/alpha and the cache dirs.
#   main      the one Main(alpha) request and the child it starts:
#             none -> checked (passed Project(), holds the per-slug lock)
#             -> persisted (mains[alpha] and meta[id].Project written)
#             -> spawned (process started; not in s.kids until claim)
#             -> booted (the child read project.yml) | exited (it could
#             not: Create fails "session exited before writing history")
#             -> live (history exists, claimed; the orb row, mounted
#             after the history row, has not read project.yml yet)
#             -> running (the orb row read it) | dead (it could not:
#             a row failed at the first mount is fatal, and the child
#             exits) ; live, running -> killed (by EndProject).
#   msg       the answer to that POST /api/projects/alpha/message.
#   mains, filed   mains[alpha] set; meta[main].Project == "alpha".
#   dele      the one DELETE /api/projects/alpha: idle -> ended
#             (EndProject done) -> emptied (RemoveAll removed the entries
#             it read) -> removed (directory, images, caches gone) | failed
#             (rmdir hit ENOTEMPTY) ; removed -> done (mains and meta
#             cleaned, 200).
#   missed    ghost: main passed its Project() check but EndProject cannot
#             end it: EndProject ran while main was between the check
#             and claim (neither MainID nor Kill sees an unclaimed child),
#             or the check landed after EndProject and before RemoveAll
#             took project.yml.
#   save      the one PUT orb/files/MEMORY.md: idle -> checked (Project()
#             and Stat(dir) passed) -> tmp (temp file created) -> ok | err.
#   agent     an agent has written ~/.bough/projects/alpha/MEMORY.md
#             (MkdirAll + write: it recreates the directory if it is gone).
#   create    the one POST /api/projects {name: "Alpha"} after the delete
#             answered: "" | ok | 409.
#
# Scope cuts: the save is of MEMORY.md (a project.yml save racing the
# delete would put project.yml back and the project reappears, its
# images and caches kept but its threads killed: a different gap); the
# agent writes only once the directory is gone (into a live project a
# MEMORY.md is ordinary, and into the emptied one it is the save's
# race again); no message is sent after the re-create (that is a new
# project's first message, project_main_threads); EndProject's container stop is folded into
# killing the child; Create's 10 s timeout is not modelled.

role Project:
    action Init:
        self.yml = True
        self.dir = True
        self.stray = False
        self.tmp = False
        self.cache = True
        self.main = "none"
        self.msg = ""
        self.mains = False
        self.filed = False
        self.dele = "idle"
        self.missed = False
        self.save = "idle"
        self.agent = False
        self.create = ""

    # --- Main(alpha), from the first message to the project.

    # messageProject: projectOr404, then Main's own Project() check and
    # the per-slug lock. Both read project.yml; folded into one step.
    atomic action MessageFirst:
        require self.main == "none" and self.msg == "" and self.create == ""
        if self.yml:
            self.main = "checked"
            # A check that lands after EndProject (before RemoveAll took
            # project.yml): nothing will end what it starts either.
            self.missed = self.dele != "idle"
        else:
            self.msg = "404"

    # Main persists the id and the membership BEFORE spawning, under s.mu
    # and without re-checking the project: a delete that finished since
    # the check gets its cleanup undone here.
    atomic fair action MainPersist:
        require self.main == "checked"
        self.mains = True
        self.filed = True
        self.main = "persisted"

    atomic fair action MainSpawn:
        require self.main == "persisted"
        self.main = "spawned"

    # cmd/bough/mode.go: a project child loads project.yml first and
    # exits without history when it cannot; Main answers that as a plain
    # error, which statusFor makes a 500.
    atomic fair action ChildBoot:
        require self.main == "spawned"
        if self.yml:
            self.main = "booted"
        else:
            self.main = "exited"
            self.msg = "500"

    # The history file appears: claim puts the child in s.kids and
    # messageProject sends the text. The pipe takes it; the child reads
    # stdin only once every row has mounted.
    atomic fair action MainHistoryAppears:
        require self.main == "booted"
        self.main = "live"
        self.msg = "ok"

    # The orb row (it needs the history row) reads project.yml again. A
    # definition gone since the boot fails the row, and a failed row at
    # the first mount is fatal: the child exits, the message unread.
    atomic fair action OrbReadsDef:
        require self.main == "live"
        if self.yml:
            self.main = "running"
        else:
            self.main = "dead"

    # The orb row's EnsureImage: MkdirAll of the image dir, whether or
    # not the project still exists.
    atomic action ChildBuildsOrb:
        require self.main == "running" and not self.cache
        self.cache = True

    # --- DeleteProject (no mainLock).

    # Project() check, then EndProject: MainID is "" until the history
    # exists, and EndChild's Kill finds nothing in s.kids before claim.
    atomic action DeleteProject:
        require self.dele == "idle" and self.yml
        self.missed = self.main in ("checked", "persisted", "spawned", "booted")
        if self.main in ("live", "running"):
            self.main = "killed"
        self.dele = "ended"

    # RemoveAll(project dir) removes the entries it read.
    atomic fair action RemoveEntries:
        require self.dele == "ended"
        self.yml = False
        self.stray = False
        self.tmp = False
        self.dele = "emptied"

    # Its rmdir, then the image and cache dirs.
    atomic fair action RemoveAllOk:
        require self.dele == "emptied" and not self.tmp and not self.stray
        self.dir = False
        self.cache = False
        self.dele = "removed"

    # An entry created after RemoveAll read the directory: ENOTEMPTY.
    # DeleteProject returns the error; images, caches, mains and meta
    # stay, and everything EndProject killed stays killed.
    atomic fair action RemoveAllFails:
        require self.dele == "emptied" and (self.tmp or self.stray)
        self.dele = "failed"

    atomic fair action CleanMeta:
        require self.dele == "removed"
        self.mains = False
        self.filed = False
        self.dele = "done"

    # --- PUT orb/files/MEMORY.md.

    # projectOr404 and WriteFile's Stat(dir).
    atomic action PutOrbFile:
        require self.save == "idle"
        if self.yml:
            self.save = "checked"
        else:
            self.save = "err"

    # atomicWrite's CreateTemp in the directory.
    atomic fair action SaveTemp:
        require self.save == "checked"
        if self.dir:
            self.tmp = True
            self.save = "tmp"
        else:
            self.save = "err"

    # The rename; the temp file may have been removed under it.
    atomic fair action SaveRename:
        require self.save == "tmp"
        if self.tmp:
            self.tmp = False
            self.stray = True
            self.save = "ok"
        else:
            self.save = "err"

    # --- an agent's file tools.

    atomic action AgentWritesFileInDir:
        require not self.agent and self.dele in ("removed", "done")
        self.agent = True
        self.dir = True
        self.stray = True

    # --- a person creates "Alpha" again once the delete has answered.

    atomic action CreateProject:
        require self.create == "" and self.dele in ("done", "failed")
        if self.dir:
            self.create = "409"
        else:
            self.dir = True
            self.yml = True
            self.create = "ok"

action Init:
    project = Project()

# --- what the product guarantees today (checked; each shown failing by a
# mutation when the flow was added).

# A child alive after a finished delete is one EndProject could not see:
# it was between Main's Project() check and claim.
always assertion OnlyAnUnseenMainOutlivesDelete:
    p = project
    return not (p.dele in ("removed", "done") and p.main in ("spawned", "booted", "live", "running")) or p.missed

# EndProject kills a main it can see.
always assertion ClaimedMainIsKilled:
    return project.dele == "idle" or project.main not in ("live", "running") or project.missed

# After a finished delete, mains and meta name the slug only when a mint
# in flight wrote them after the cleanup.
always assertion OnlyAnInFlightMintRefiles:
    p = project
    return p.dele != "done" or not (p.mains or p.filed) or p.missed

# A directory without project.yml holds something a writer put there
# after RemoveAll read it (the moment between RemoveAll's two halves
# aside, and a delete that failed after removing project.yml).
always assertion ZombieHoldsAWrite:
    p = project
    return not (p.dir and not p.yml) or p.dele == "emptied" or p.stray or p.tmp

# Create is refused by the directory, whatever the list shows.
always assertion CreateRefusedByDirOnly:
    return project.create != "409" or project.dir

# The message is answered ok only when main's history exists.
always assertion MessageOkMeansHistory:
    return project.msg != "ok" or project.main in ("live", "running", "dead", "killed")

# Every request in flight answers, and the list catches up.
always eventually assertion RequestsAnswer:
    p = project
    return (p.main not in ("checked", "persisted", "spawned", "booted")
            and p.dele not in ("ended", "emptied", "removed")
            and p.save not in ("checked", "tmp"))

# --- what it should guarantee and does not (fizz finds each violated
# on this spec; kept as comments so the graph can be generated):
#
# After a delete, no child runs with BOUGH_PROJECT=alpha:
#   return project.dele not in ("removed", "done") or project.main not in ("spawned", "booted", "live", "running")
# After a delete, mains and meta have no entry for the slug:
#   return project.dele != "done" or not (project.mains or project.filed)
# A directory the list does not show never makes Create 409:
#   return project.create != "409" or project.yml
# A failed delete leaves the project whole or gone:
#   return project.dele != "failed" or project.yml or not project.dir
# A message to a project deleted mid-request answers 404/409:
#   return project.msg != "500" and not (project.msg == "ok" and project.dele != "idle" and not project.yml)
# A delete leaves no image or cache dir for the slug:
#   return project.dele != "done" or project.create == "ok" or not project.cache
# Liveness: a delete racing a boot eventually leaves nothing running:
#   always eventually: not (project.dele == "done" and project.main in ("spawned", "booted", "live", "running"))
# Liveness: a zombie directory is eventually listed or removable:
#   always eventually: not (project.dir and not project.yml)
